# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for LRPS2 sweeps.
#
# Usage:
#   TSAN_OPTIONS="suppressions=tests/tsan.supp" <harness>
#
# Two categories only.  Anything TSan reports that is not matched here
# is NEW and must be triaged, not added blindly.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# ACCEPTED BY DESIGN - do not "fix" without an architecture decision.
#
# The EE thread writes GS privileged registers (SMODE1/SMODE2, PMODE,
# DISPFB, ...) directly into shared PS2MEM_GS via gsWrite64_page_00 /
# gsWrite64_generic; the GS side reads them at vsync (GSRenderer::Merge,
# GSState::GetVideoMode / isReallyInterlaced, MTGS::MainLoop's vsync
# path).  Inherited from upstream PCSX2, where priv-reg traffic is
# deliberately not ring-serialized.  Accesses are aligned and
# word-sized on the only supported host (x86-64: single mov, no
# tearing); worst case is a one-frame-stale video mode, which matches
# real-hardware semantics - a mode change mid-scanout is "torn" on a
# real PS2 too.  Serializing these through the MTGS ring would be
# invasive, perf-relevant, and upstream-divergent.
race:GSState::GetVideoMode
race:GSState::isReallyInterlaced
race:gsWrite64_generic
race:gsWrite64_page_00
race:MTGS::MainLoop
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# TRACKED - genuine bug class, NOT yet root-caused.
#
# GS local memory is written from two directions without reliable
# mutual exclusion: a host->local transfer on the GS/EE side
# (WriteImageX -> WritePixel4HH and friends, read-modify-write) racing
# an in-flight SW rasterizer draw on a worker thread (DrawRectT /
# FillBlock, 8-byte stores) at the SAME address.
#
# This is NOT a worker-vs-worker sub-word packing problem, and it is
# NOT fixable with an atomic RMW or by widening scanline ownership -
# an earlier note in this file said so and was wrong.  GSRendererSW
# already has the intended mechanism: InvalidateVideoMem /
# InvalidateLocalMem consult m_fzb_pages / m_tex_pages and call
# Sync() when a transfer touches pages the rasterizer is using.  A
# race reaching WritePixel4HH means that page tracking has a GAP -
# wrong page set for the rect, a transfer path that skips the
# Invalidate call, or a tracking update ordered after the transfer.
#
# Next step is therefore diagnostic, not a fix: instrument the
# Invalidate paths to assert that every page touched by a transfer is
# either untracked or Sync()'d first, and find which transfer slips
# through.  Only then does a fix (and its FPS measurement) make
# sense.  User-visible symptom today is rare corrupted texels/pixels
# in content that streams textures while drawing.
race:GSLocalMemory::WritePixel4HH
race:GSLocalMemory::WritePixel4HL
race:GSLocalMemory::WritePixel8H
race:GSRasterizer::Draw
